  "mapping": {
    "authored_date": "2026-07-18",
    "deviation_notes": "The cold-arrow-with-cone-splash-behind-target identity lands cleanly via cone geometry + water + ELEMENT_CONVERSION_PHYSICAL + freeze/shatter, with only minor drift: the skill is a two-part hit (partial phys->cold ON the target, then TOTAL phys->cold in the cone behind it) and the engine expresses the dominant cone while the on-target partial-conversion hit is folded into the cone-delivery note rather than modeled as a separate strike. A player keeps the aim-the-cone-through-the-pack cold-archer feel; the exact split between the single-target arrow hit and the full-conversion cone is generalized to the cone as the identity footprint.",
    "grade": "CLOSE",
    "kit_id": "poe1-ice-shot",
    "mapping_json": {
      "fidelity_notes": "CONE-BEHIND-TARGET cold archer. Geometry cone -- dossier is explicit: 'converts all physical to cold in a CONE behind that target, base radius 2.4m'; the cone-splash IS the identity (crosswalk s6 'cone/breath/sweep -> cone'), the arrow is the vector into it. Modeled with cone as the dominant geometry (what clears the pack every shot); extra-arrows/projectile-count for Deadeye clear noted in traits (multi_projectile is the secondary clear-scaling lane, not the identity footprint). water/cold family; chill+freeze (native shatter payoff). ELEMENT_CONVERSION_PHYSICAL is the capstone door -- Ice Shot's defining act is converting physical to cold (partial on-target, TOTAL in the cone; crosswalk s5 phys-to-X). ELEMENTAL_ECHO for the mono-cold amp. Asenath's Mark (auto hex/exposure/mark) + Returning Projectiles (hit twice) are endgame item accelerants noted in geometry/economy, not identity. The cone-behind-target aiming skill (line up the cone through a pack) is preserved by the cone geometry.",
      "motion_frame": "cold archer: fire arrows into packs, each impact blooms a cold cone behind the struck enemy that freezes and chills the group -- a ranged clear playstyle built around aiming the cone through enemies",
      "option_c_substrate_flags": null,
      "resource_economy": {},
